{
  "fileVersion": "1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Membrane Template",
    "description": "Three chained Membrane nodes authoring a real custom boundary -- a quadrilateral, not the default rectangle. The chain must close (declaration.boundary-begin -> membrane -> ...-> membrane.next -> declaration.boundary-end) to resolve at all; an open chain falls back to a plain rectangle, same as having no Membrane nodes.",
    "graphId": "membrane-template-declaration",
    "version": "0.2.3",
    "kind": "template",
    "created": "2026-10-04T20:18:22.272Z",
    "modified": "2026-10-06T20:35:37.839Z",
    "author": "",
    "tags": [
      "template",
      "membrane"
    ],
    "preferredViewer": "https://dev.twilite.zone"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "membrane-template-declaration",
      "type": "declaration",
      "label": "Membrane Template",
      "root": true,
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -600
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 240,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "membrane-template-declaration",
          "name": "Membrane Template",
          "version": "0.2.3",
          "description": "Three chained Membrane nodes authoring a real custom boundary -- a quadrilateral, not the default rectangle. The chain must close (declaration.boundary-begin -> membrane -> ...-> membrane.next -> declaration.boundary-end) to resolve at all; an open chain falls back to a plain rectangle, same as having no Membrane nodes."
        },
        "intent": {
          "kind": "template",
          "scope": "local"
        },
        "declaration": {
          "kind": "graph",
          "defaultSurfaceId": "web",
          "surfaces": []
        },
        "glyph": {
          "kind": "icon",
          "name": "Shield"
        },
        "name": "Declaration",
        "purpose": "",
        "document": {
          "url": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/membrane-template/root.node"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "membrane-template-content",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Content",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 400
      },
      "width": 460,
      "height": 340,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "membrane-template",
          "nodeId": "membrane-template-content"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:28px;background:#ffffff;font-family:system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow:auto'><h1 style='margin:0 0 12px;font:800 24px/1.2 system-ui'>Membrane</h1><p style='margin:0 0 12px;max-width:62ch;font:400 15px/1.6 system-ui;color:#334155'>Each Membrane node has exactly two ports: <strong>root</strong> ('boundary in', left, input) receives the chain from whatever precedes it -- the Declaration's boundary-begin relationship for the first one, or the previous Membrane's next for every one after. <strong>next</strong> ('boundary next', right, output) hands off to whatever continues the chain -- another Membrane, or, on the last one, back to the Declaration's boundary-end. A chain that doesn't close at boundary-end isn't a custom boundary at all -- it falls back to the default rectangle, the same as a graph with no Membrane nodes.</p><p style='margin:0 0 12px;max-width:62ch;font:400 15px/1.6 system-ui;color:#334155'><strong>Known limitation, confirmed by reading the code, not assumed:</strong> once a graph contains any real Membrane node, dragging a workspace tile's resize handle stops working, for every such graph, with no exception for a real, closed chain like this one. <code>resizeGraphMembrane</code> (graphWorkspace.js) does write the new size to <code>declaration.data.membrane.bounds</code> on every drag -- but <code>graphRenderBounds</code> and, separately, <code>resolveAuthoredInterfaceFrame</code> (interfaceFrame.js) each compute <code>hasControls = nodes.some(n => n.type === 'membrane')</code> and, whenever that's true, never read <code>declaration.data.membrane.bounds</code> back -- the frame is instead inferred from the distance and direction between the Declaration node and its landing-surface Content node, scaled by the declaration's aspect ratio. The resize write lands; it's just never consulted again. To actually resize a Membrane-bounded graph's tile, move the Declaration and/or its landing-surface node further apart or closer together in the editor -- dragging the workspace corner handle is a no-op from the very next render on.</p></div>"
        }
      }
    },
